<title>LATVIA: Latvian trade deficit rises in Jan-Sept 1996.</title>
<headline>Latvian trade deficit rises in Jan-Sept 1996.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvia's trade deficit, calculated in real prices and which do not strip out inflation, rose in the first nine months of the year compared to a year ago and the January to August period, the statistics committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Inflation in September was 0.7 percent month-on-month and 16.2 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>LATVIAN TRADE BALANCE</p>
<p>		Jan-Sept '96  Jan-Aug '96   Jan-Sept '95</p>
<p>    Exports  579.10	  509.19	   496.70</p>
<p>    Imports  894.12	  786.74	   673.10</p>
<p>    Deficit  315.02	  277.55	   176.40</p>
<p>Note -- all figures are in millions of lats.</p>
<p>Largest export destinations as percentage of total exports versus same period last year:</p>
<p>Russia  -  23.3 (25.0)</p>
<p>Germany -  13.9 (14.3)</p>
<p>Britain -  10.6 (9.7)</p>
<p>Largest source of imports as percentage of total imports versus same period last year:</p>
<p>Russia  - 19.1 (21.1)</p>
<p>Germany - 14.1 (15.7)</p>
<p>Finland -  9.6 (10.8)</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
